# 3 readings by claude-opus-5-5, compared
mill-subjection-4.md:1: argue/readings: S2 is read 2 ways: mill-subjection-4.logic.r2 and mill-subjection-4.logic.r2.3 have nothing from it; mill-subjection-4.logic.r2.2 has "liberate → women_free"; they differ when only "the world ceases to make sex a disqualification for privileges and a badge of subjection" is true, which the first allows
mill-subjection-4.md:1: argue/answered: S2: answered no, which keeps mill-subjection-4.logic.r2.2, to: Suppose "the world ceases to make sex a disqualification for privileges and a badge of subjection" is true and "women have a life of rational freedom rather than a life of subjection to the will of others" is false. Is S2, "But it would be a grievous understatement of the case to omit the most direct benefit of all, the unspeakable gain in private happiness to the liberated half of the species; the difference to them between a life of subjection to the will of others, and a life of rational freedom.", true then?
mill-subjection-4.md:1: argue/readings: S5 is read 2 ways: mill-subjection-4.logic.r2 has nothing from it; mill-subjection-4.logic.r2.2 and mill-subjection-4.logic.r2.3 have "desire_not_less ∧ reject_others_will"; they differ when only "those who have learnt the meaning of duty and the value of reason do not desire freedom less" is true, which the first allows
mill-subjection-4.md:1: argue/answered: S5: answered no, which keeps mill-subjection-4.logic.r2.2 and mill-subjection-4.logic.r2.3, to: Suppose "those who have learnt the meaning of duty and the value of reason do not desire freedom less" is true and "those who have learnt duty and reason are not disposed to accept the will of other people as the interpreter of their guiding principles" is false. Is S5, "When they have learnt to understand the meaning of duty and the value of reason, they incline more and more to be guided and restrained by these in the exercise of their freedom; but they do not therefore desire freedom less; they do not become disposed to accept the will of other people as the representative and interpreter of those guiding principles.", true then?
mill-subjection-4.logic.r2: argue/readings: what the text leaves unstated is read 3 ways: mill-subjection-4.logic.r2 has "cultivated_assert_freedom → desire_not_less ∧ reject_others_will" and "liberate → women_free" and "women_free ∧ freedom_strongest_want ∧ desire_not_less ∧ reject_others_will → gain_happiness"; mill-subjection-4.logic.r2.2 has "freedom_strongest_want ∧ desire_not_less ∧ reject_others_will ∧ cultivated_assert_freedom → (women_free → gain_happiness)"; they differ when only "the world ceases to make sex a disqualification for privileges and a badge of subjection", "women have a life of rational freedom rather than a life of subjection to the will of others", "there is an unspeakable gain in private happiness to the liberated half of the species", "after the primary necessities of food and raiment, freedom is the first and strongest want of human nature", "those who have learnt the meaning of duty and the value of reason do not desire freedom less" and "the communities in which reason has been most cultivated and social duty most powerful are those which have most strongly asserted the freedom of action of the individual" are true, which the second allows; mill-subjection-4.logic.r2.3 has "liberate → women_free" and "women_free ∧ freedom_strongest_want ∧ desire_not_less ∧ reject_others_will → gain_happiness"
